msgctxt "64"
msgid "How to Play Eight-ball"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "76"
msgid "Eight-ball uses balls number 1 through 15."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "88"
msgid ""
"Balls 1 through 7 are called Low Balls, while balls\r\n"
"9 through 15 are called High Balls."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "100"
msgid ""
"The first ball a player sinks after the break shot decides\r\n"
"which group of balls will be theirs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "112"
msgid ""
"To win, you must pocket the 8 ball after pocketing all of\r\n"
"the balls in your group."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "124"
msgid "You can pocket the balls in your group in any order."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "136"
msgid ""
"Before sinking the 8 ball, you must specify which pocket\r\n"
"you are aiming for."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "148"
msgid "Sinking it in any other pocket results in an automatic loss."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "160"
msgid ""
"Pocketing the 8 ball before all of the balls in your group\r\n"
"have been sunk also counts as a loss."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "172"
msgid "Fouls"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "184"
msgid ""
"A foul results if the cue ball falls into a pocket or does\r\n"
"not strike an object ball."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "196"
msgid ""
"The opposing player may then take a shot by placing the cue\r\n"
"ball anywhere on the table."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "208"
msgid "Now, let's give it a try."
msgstr ""